Negative control for the sort offer being the REAL, TITLED columns
(`R6-6` · `R6-6b` · `R6-28`).

Puts the query schema's sort vocabulary back to a bare, untitled enum naming
`created_at` · `email` · `default`. Nothing declares the boolean columns the
ruling named (`verified`, `bounced`), and a bare enum can title nothing, so the
control offers two options under their WIRE names — the live defect this
replaced. The status composite stays absent either way, which is the half of
`R6-6b` this must not be able to claim credit for.

Apply from the repo root: `git apply <this file>`; revert with `git apply -R`.

Reds: the sort-offer spec — the control offers the schema's declared sort
columns under the schema's own titles, and no option renders as a wire name.

diff --git a/packages/headless/src/modules/client-email/client-email.schemas.ts b/packages/headless/src/modules/client-email/client-email.schemas.ts
--- a/packages/headless/src/modules/client-email/client-email.schemas.ts
+++ b/packages/headless/src/modules/client-email/client-email.schemas.ts
@@ -199,20 +199,7 @@ export function useQuerySchema(): QuerySchema {
           additionalProperties: false,
           required: ["field", "dir"],
           properties: {
-            // `oneOf` const/title, not a bare enum: the sort control's option
-            // labels are the schema's own titles (`R6-28`), and a bare enum can
-            // carry none — which is what left `created_at` and `default`
-            // rendering as wire names. The columns are the REAL ones the API
-            // orders on, the status composite never among them (`R6-6`/`R6-6b`).
-            field: {
-              oneOf: [
-                { const: "default", title: "text.default_label" },
-                { const: "email", title: "text.email_address" },
-                { const: "verified", title: "text.verified_label" },
-                { const: "bounced", title: "text.bounced_label" },
-                { const: "created_at", title: "text.date_added" }
-              ]
-            },
+            field: { enum: ["created_at", "email", "default"] },
             dir: { enum: [SortDirection.ASC, SortDirection.DESC] }
           }
         }
